  "intentNotInMockup": [
    "Status bar, Dynamic Island and home indicator are simulated drawings; the OS draws the real ones",
    "Tab bar is an opaque white fallback; on iOS 26 use the native tab bar with Regular Liquid Glass (opaque under Reduce Transparency)",
    "Sheets are drawn statically; native modal sheet with grabber, swipe-down dismissal and 260 ms rise",
    "First-confirmation check draw (220 ms, motion.easeOut; Reduce Motion 120 ms opacity) is prototyped in HTML (r3a; .check-draw) and observed in browser seek and wall-clock samples (evidence/capture-ledger.json r3aCapture.groups.M); it is not visible in still refs. The optional light haptic (expo-haptics) is native-only",
    "r3b corrected the live HTML confirm path (D8-2/D8-3), proved by root live stills W1-W6 (evidence/receipts/r3b/live/): m:ss timer from a stored end time, Set N+1 current while resting, timer accessible name from the live value. Native: compute remaining time from the stored end time on every foreground/AppState change, update the accessibilityLabel with the visible text, and do not announce every second (VoiceOver reads the timer on focus); announcement cadence is native intent, unproved",
    "Rest timer counts real elapsed time and recomputes on foreground; renders freeze at 0:48",
    "Implementation follow-ups, unknown in this package and not design decisions: native haptics, Liquid Glass, sheet physics, keyboard avoidance, VoiceOver announcement cadence and native Dynamic Type metrics; browser motion timing is not native timing. Prove them natively",
    "The Workout figure is the single owned asset open-mat-squat.svg for every movement (D10-1: it shows a squat under Dumbbell floor press). Implement it exactly as specified; do not draw per-movement art or hide it on your own",
    "Numeric keyboard, focus ring behaviour and keyboard avoidance for Coach composer are not shown",
    "Coach composer (CMP-A16): implement as a multiline TextInput at every text size (the HTML keeps a single-line input at default size only because the placeholder fits one line there; the large-text refs show the wrapped form). Height grows with content or placeholder from the 56 composer up to layout.composer.maxTextHeight 144 of text, then scrolls inside. accessibilityLabel 'Message the demo coach' is persistent; the placeholder is a hint, never the label. Return key Send submits. Keyboard-safe: the accessory (footnote + composer at default size; composer only at accessibility sizes) rides above the keyboard (KeyboardAvoidingView or keyboard layout guide; the tab bar sits under the keyboard), and the scroll view's bottom inset equals the measured accessory top, so the latest message stays visible",
    "v2 Coach rules (space-shape, r4): the context line 'Today: Full-body strength, 35 minutes', the Review primary and the 'I have 20 minutes' prompt render only while today's plan is the full 35-minute plan (they describe or offer it). After Apply the thread follows the title (s20), and the success Notice with Undo replaces the CTA (contract item 8), followed only by 'Why these movements?'. Undo restores the context line and both prompts; while a Notice shows, Review stays hidden (v1 rule)",
    "v2 Coach at accessibility sizes: the accessory is the composer alone (padding s8 top and bottom); the footnote 'Sample replies, on this device.' is the last item of the scroll content (t-meta secondary, s16 after the prompts). Default size is unchanged: footnote pinned in the accessory, bottom padding layout.composer.outerGap 16",
    "v2 Plan rest day: the selected plan panel holds only the rest day (empty mat, date, 'Thursday is a rest day.', 'Your next strength session is Friday.'). Below it on the canvas (s24) a SessionSummary (CMP-A07) for the next planned day: 'Next: Friday, Oct 9', 'Full-body strength', '35 minutes 5 movements 11 sets', then (s20) the primary 'See Friday's workout' (a-plan-primary, selects Friday)",
    "v2 WeeklyChart zero state (every week 0, progress.empty): value, baseline and date only; the chart height is its content (no layout.chart.height reserve), so no empty bar band. Values stay printed",
    "Coach scroll inset: the scroll view ends at the measured top of the composer accessory at every text size (onLayout). layout.composer.scrollBottom 199 is a superseded mockup estimate (it assumed a 56 composer; the rendered default accessory is 115, composer 62); do not hard-code it",
    "Lucide icons are used directly in RN (lucide-react-native); SF Symbol names are listed only for a future SwiftUI consumer",
    "accessibility-large refs (refs/accessibility-large/) use a uniform 2.0 text multiplier (display capped 1.5), an approximation near iOS AX2, not native Dynamic Type",
    "HTML font rasterisation differs from iOS CoreText; numeric fidelity must be checked natively"
  ],
