  "refinements": [
    "Metadata strings use spaced items (metaline, 16 column gap) instead of middle dots (\"35 minutes   5 movements   11 sets\"); they stack at large text.",
    "Plan's \"Today\" marker reads \"Today, Wednesday, Oct 7\" in the panel's date line.",
    "Coach context line reads \"Today: Full-body strength, 35 minutes\".",
    "Rest days and empty Progress use the empty-mat silhouette (the system's optional EmptyErrorBlock art), giving the signature a meaning: nobody on the mat yet.",
    "Resting state: Notice + RestPanel with \"Skip rest\"; after skip or expiry the panel is replaced by \"Start set N\". No primary competes with the timer while counting.",
    "Progress summary rows cut their optional icons (recorded as the removed accessory in critique).",
    "Progress history toggle (r3b, D8-1): the contract's item 4 called it a primary, but the same item says it “simply controls disclosure”, and the component hierarchy keeps the one filled primary for the screen's main action. It is now a PlainAction with chevron-down / chevron-up and an expanded state. Progress default therefore has no filled primary (reading screen); Progress empty keeps “Go to workout”.",
    "Bodyweight load (r3b): a suggested 0 kg reads “body weight” (“12 reps   body weight”; “12 × body weight”), never “0 kg”. The Weight field still edits added kilograms.",
    "Live rest copy (r3b, D8-2/D8-3): after a set is confirmed, set N+1 is current and the panel reads “Set N+1 starts when you choose.”; after a movement's last set it names the next movement (“Dumbbell floor press starts when you choose.”, primary “Start Dumbbell floor press”). That boundary copy is a working assumption filling an unspecified case with the existing verb pattern.",
    "Selected chart week: the contract's 2 pt ink outline never crosses the baseline (round 1, kept). In round 2 each of the selected week's blocks carries the 2 pt ink edge inside its own box.",
    "Today: “1 of 3 workouts recorded” is trailing meta on the “This week” row; measured DayPicker y 669–751, 33 pt clear of the tab bar (round 1, kept). Large text keeps the stacked plain link.",
    "Round 2 (kept after the r2 capture on plan, coach and progress), each documented with before/after in critique.md:",
    "Coach header shows only “Coach”. The contract's trailing “Demo coach” meta was a third disclosure on one screen; the label stays on every coach message (CMP-A14 “always visible”) and the footnote “Sample replies, on this device.” stays above the composer, so the demo meaning is unchanged.",
    "Coach seeded line reads “Short on time? Keep the main three.” (one line) instead of the two-line contract sentence; the numbered proposal now names the three movements.",
    "Coach proposal lists the short plan as three numbered compact rows (Goblet squat 3 sets, Dumbbell floor press 2 sets, One-arm dumbbell row 2 sets) with metadata “7 planned sets   15 minutes shorter”, replacing the prose “Squat, floor press and row. 7 planned sets.”, which left an orphaned word.",
    "Plan and the exercise list number movements 1–5 in workout order (Bricolage numerals), echoing Workout's “Movement 1 of 5” and the class whiteboard.",
    "WeeklyChart draws each recorded workout as one stacked block instead of a continuous bar: “Look what adds up” is literally countable, and the count never reads as a performance score.",
    "Round 3 (kept after the r3 capture; the last allowed loop):",
    "Coach uses one 16 pt rhythm from the thread down to the prompts (the proposal-to-action gap goes from 20 to 16), and the proposal has 16 vertical padding. In r2 the first prompt’s bottom (671) sat 2 pt under the composer zone (top 669), so its border was cut. Expected: proposal [24, 341, 354, 178], Review y 535, first prompt [24, 609, …, 50], 10 pt clear.",
    "Chart block corners go from 12 to 8.",
    "v2, source r4 (a disclosed fourth creative cycle, space-shape only; existing tokens, components and assets; no new value). Written as predictions; root's r4 capture (v2 session 12) matched every predicted frame on both phones, and the refs are now these r4 captures:",
    "Coach with the 20-minute plan applied from Plan or Today, then opened: the current applied layout stands (title → thread → proposal → “Why these movements?”; no context line, no Review, no “I have 20 minutes”). The plan state is already shown by the 20-minute proposal, by the Notice and Undo when applied here, and by Today and Plan. No extra context line is added: it would be a new copy pattern for a state the existing surfaces already state (coordinator disposition, session 12)."
  ],
